<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>RFI - All the news from France, Europe, Africa and the rest of the world.</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Sat, 01 Aug 2026 11:49:32 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Sports</category><title>Fifa boss Infantino scraps plan to sell off World Cup profits to private equity</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260801-fifa-boss-infantino-scraps-plan-to-sell-off-world-cup-profits-to-private-equity-world-cup-2026</link><description>
Gianni Infantino, the boss of world football's governing body Fifa, caved in to international pressure on Saturday and abandoned his brainchild to sell World Cup profits to private equity.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6187729e-8d3a-11f1-919e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-28T162945Z-1037867588-RC28KJAED3SY-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-FIFA-STAKE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6187729e-8d3a-11f1-919e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-28T162945Z-1037867588-RC28KJAED3SY-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-FIFA-STAKE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a71431d2-8d7e-11f1-91b7-f716cf42b3e4</guid><pubDate>Sat, 01 Aug 2026 09:34:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6187729e-8d3a-11f1-919e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-28T162945Z-1037867588-RC28KJAED3SY-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-FIFA-STAKE.jpg">© Benoit Tessier / REUTERS</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>No go for Infantino: How Fifa's World Cup private investment plan imploded</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260801-no-go-for-infantino-how-fifa-s-world-cup-private-investment-plan-imploded</link><description>
The planet's most powerful football administrator Gianni Infantino on Saturday yielded to the international collective when he pulled the plug on a plan to allow private investment in the World Cup. His proposals for world football's governing body Fifa to reform its commercial operations had sparked a furious backlash.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f31c9020-8445-11f1-8a7b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-20T000943Z-1234957518-UP1EM7J1UL3TE-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-WORLDCUP-ESP-ARG.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f31c9020-8445-11f1-8a7b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-20T000943Z-1234957518-UP1EM7J1UL3TE-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-WORLDCUP-ESP-ARG.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">53e5b36e-8d97-11f1-9812-fffbeee1baf8</guid><pubDate>Sat, 01 Aug 2026 11:41:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f31c9020-8445-11f1-8a7b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-20T000943Z-1234957518-UP1EM7J1UL3TE-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-WORLDCUP-ESP-ARG.jpg">REUTERS - Lee Smith</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Africa's top cocoa producers pledge fairer prices for farmers</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260801-africa-s-top-cocoa-producers-pledge-fairer-prices-for-farmers</link><description>
Ghana and Côte d'Ivoire, the world's two largest cocoa producers, have signed a joint declaration pledging closer cooperation on pricing, local processing, environmental protection and scientific research, as the two countries seek to secure better incomes for millions of cocoa farmers
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0e21b5d6-8cf6-11f1-a4b0-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Picture-1-1-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0e21b5d6-8cf6-11f1-a4b0-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Picture-1-1-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d5be2b2c-8cf8-11f1-95ed-d172a205da8e</guid><pubDate>Sat, 01 Aug 2026 10:13:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0e21b5d6-8cf6-11f1-a4b0-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Picture-1-1-1.jpg">© Presidency of Ghana</source><dc:creator>Michael Sarpong Mfum in Ghana</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Burkina Faso added to human rights watchlist over crackdown on civil society</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260801-burkina-faso-added-to-human-rights-watchlist-over-crackdown-on-civil-society</link><description>
Burkina Faso has been added to the watchlist of human rights monitoring NGO Civicus, with the country's military authorities drastically escalating restrictions on civil society and intensifying reprisals against its critics in recent months.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a43a6e84-80ce-11f1-a332-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Burkina-Faso-Traore.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a43a6e84-80ce-11f1-a332-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Burkina-Faso-Traore.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">617e717a-8b33-11f1-891d-f1977c9499c6</guid><pubDate>Sat, 01 Aug 2026 11:48:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a43a6e84-80ce-11f1-a332-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Burkina-Faso-Traore.jpg">AP - Stanislav Krasilnikov</source><dc:creator>Melissa Chemam</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Women's Tour de France pits France's Ferrand-Prévot against history</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260801-women-s-tour-de-france-pits-france-s-ferrand-pr%C3%A9vot-against-history</link><description>
France's star cyclist Pauline Ferrand-Prévot will set off on Saturday as one of the favourites for the 2026 Women's Tour de France. The 34-year-old will also be seeking a slice of cycling history. No rider has retained the crown since the competition started in 2022.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/06aec6e8-8ce4-11f1-ad6a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/tour-de-france.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/06aec6e8-8ce4-11f1-ad6a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/tour-de-france.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9e36423c-8ccd-11f1-b296-69bfde5d3c03</guid><pubDate>Sat, 01 Aug 2026 07:29:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/06aec6e8-8ce4-11f1-ad6a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/tour-de-france.jpg">Jean-Christophe Bott/Keystone vi - Jean-Christophe Bott</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>'Humanitarian emergency' as influx of migrants overwhelms Spanish enclave Ceuta</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260731-humanitarian-emergency-as-influx-of-migrants-overwhelms-spanish-enclave-ceuta</link><description>
Some 60,000 migrants entered Spain’s north African enclave of Ceuta from Morocco in the space of 24 hours, between Thursday and Friday, leaving at least 34 dead and prompting France to tighten controls along its border with Spain.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8731f13c-8cb7-11f1-abbb-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26211730761972.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8731f13c-8cb7-11f1-abbb-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26211730761972.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2942eb1a-8cb9-11f1-aa04-51f91fa6bfb9</guid><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 16:20:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8731f13c-8cb7-11f1-abbb-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26211730761972.jpg">AP Photo/Antonio Sempere - Antonio Sempere</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>As Bordeaux blaze eases, Ukraine sends reinforcements to France</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260731-as-bordeaux-blaze-eases-ukraine-sends-reinforcements-to-france</link><description>
French Interior Minister Laurent Nunez said on Friday that 308 people have been detained nationwide over the wildfire outbreak, with two-thirds suspected of "deliberate arson". The announcement came as the blaze near Bordeaux showed signs of easing and Ukraine dispatched 70 rescuers to help battle the fires still burning across France.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/59b16258-8c65-11f1-b551-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3KT7NQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/59b16258-8c65-11f1-b551-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3KT7NQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f47b3dd6-8cc9-11f1-8be2-69bfde5d3c03</guid><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 12:37:43 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/59b16258-8c65-11f1-b551-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3KT7NQ.jpg">AFP - OLIVIER MORIN</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France freezes assets of controversial Russian commentator Fedorova</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260731-france-freezes-assets-of-controversial-russian-commentator-fedorova</link><description>
France has frozen the assets of pro-Kremlin commentator Xenia Fedorova for six months, the government announced on Friday, adding a financial measure to an expulsion order already issued against her over accusations of spreading Kremlin propaganda on French television and undermining democracy.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/26c68814-5d9e-11f1-b4cc-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B4B2768.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/26c68814-5d9e-11f1-b4cc-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B4B2768.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9029b4b2-8cb9-11f1-a844-61d85c6ac758</guid><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 09:58:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/26c68814-5d9e-11f1-b4cc-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B4B2768.jpg">© XAVIER GALIANA / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Where you live could decide how well you breathe, French study finds</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260731-where-you-live-could-decide-how-well-you-breathe-french-study-finds-pollution-heatwave-environment</link><description>
Repeated heatwaves in France are taking a toll on people's lungs, doctors say, with young patients with no prior respiratory issues increasingly being admitted to hospital, a leading pulmonologist has told RFI.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f0301676-6554-11f1-bbb5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-19T230436Z-275179907-RC21LFAG663J-RTRMADP-3-CLIMATE-CHANGE-BRITAIN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f0301676-6554-11f1-bbb5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-19T230436Z-275179907-RC21LFAG663J-RTRMADP-3-CLIMATE-CHANGE-BRITAIN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">716c7d5c-8bf6-11f1-a43f-2390f09169c1</guid><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 06:20:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f0301676-6554-11f1-bbb5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-19T230436Z-275179907-RC21LFAG663J-RTRMADP-3-CLIMATE-CHANGE-BRITAIN.jpg">REUTERS - Temilade Adelaja</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>French national's spying conviction upheld by Azerbaijan court</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260731-french-national-s-spying-conviction-upheld-by-azerbaijan-court</link><description>
An Azerbaijani appeal court has upheld the 10-year sentence of a French national, Martin Ryan, for “espionage", in a case that arose against a backdrop of tensions between Paris and Baku. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d73f91e0-6f83-11f0-8755-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP72253799240-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d73f91e0-6f83-11f0-8755-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP72253799240-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9043fa1e-8bf3-11f1-8217-377d54a72fad</guid><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 20:39:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d73f91e0-6f83-11f0-8755-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP72253799240-1.jpg">AP - Luca Bruno</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International report</category><title>Fears of wheat price surge amid Ukraine-Russia clashes in the Black Sea</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/podcasts/international-report/20260731-fears-of-wheat-price-surge-amid-ukraine-russia-clashes-in-the-black-sea</link><description>
Intensifying clashes between Ukraine and Russia in the Black Sea are threatening a crucial trade artery responsible for nearly a third of the world's wheat supply, stoking fears of soaring prices and shortages.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/afa92442-844b-11f1-9ca2-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26200564414743.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/afa92442-844b-11f1-9ca2-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26200564414743.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c468ccd0-8cdd-11f1-aaf0-0b9b6fc7e5a3</guid><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 21:20:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dorian Jones</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>In flood-prone Malawi, bananas become a shield against erosion</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260731-in-flood-prone-malawi-bananas-become-a-shield-against-erosion</link><description>
When Davie Kampira, 34, a farmer in Nsanje, southern Malawi, received 34 banana suckers in 2024, he did not envisage that the few dozen plants he tried out on a run-down piece of land, previously used for brickmaking, would transform into a small estate. Today, two years later, the land beside the river has produced nine hectares of different banana varieties, along with houses, a shop and a better life for his two children and wife.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6a328a16-8cd9-11f1-bd6e-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Enerst-Kambiya-from-Concern-Worldwide-appreciates-Kampira-s-farm.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6a328a16-8cd9-11f1-bd6e-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Enerst-Kambiya-from-Concern-Worldwide-appreciates-Kampira-s-farm.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c51703ee-8cc0-11f1-a656-2db2fff5973b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 20:29:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6a328a16-8cd9-11f1-bd6e-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Enerst-Kambiya-from-Concern-Worldwide-appreciates-Kampira-s-farm.jpg">© RFI/Charles ,Pensulo</source><dc:creator>Charles Pensulo in Malawi</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Russia seeks arrest of Telegram's Durov over 'terrorism complicity' claims</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260730-russia-seeks-arrest-of-telegram-s-durov-over-terrorism-complicity-claims</link><description>
Russia has announced it is seeking the arrest of Telegram founder Pavel Durov over accusations of "complicity in terrorism", alleging he allowed the platform to be used for recruitment by Ukraine's security services.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/830ba85c-e3b9-11f0-a7a9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-79ZR2NE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/830ba85c-e3b9-11f0-a7a9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-79ZR2NE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e17ed11c-8bec-11f1-bd7a-8319c63ffefc</guid><pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 11:34:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/830ba85c-e3b9-11f0-a7a9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-79ZR2NE.jpg">© AFP - GIUSEPPE CACACE</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>EU crisis chief calls for prevention funding as wildfire crisis rages on</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260730-eu-crisis-chief-calls-for-prevention-funding-as-french-wildfire-crisis-rages-on</link><description>
As firefighters continue to battle major blazes in France, the European Union's crisis management chief is calling for more investment in prevention, forest management and emergency response.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/58ff3cae-8b4d-11f1-889a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-32GE7UL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/58ff3cae-8b4d-11f1-889a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-32GE7UL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4f27780a-8b4c-11f1-b52e-bd6005b43734</guid><pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 06:16:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/58ff3cae-8b4d-11f1-889a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-32GE7UL.jpg">AFP - PHILIPPE LOPEZ</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>DRC court clears path to change a constitution that says it can't be changed</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260730-drc-court-clears-path-to-change-a-constitution-that-says-it-can-t-be-changed</link><description>
The Democratic Republic of Congo's Constitutional Court has approved a referendum law that critics say could pave the way for President Felix Tshisekedi to seek a third term in office, prompting a coalition of opposition parties to reject the ruling and vow to fight the change.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9988064a-8b41-11f1-87f3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/FotoJet-74.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9988064a-8b41-11f1-87f3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/FotoJet-74.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c8a9bce2-8bfb-11f1-afa4-e32b91ea1800</guid><pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 14:07:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9988064a-8b41-11f1-87f3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/FotoJet-74.jpg"><![CDATA[© Photos AFP & AP - Montage RFI]]></source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Migrant exodus leaves South African employers short-handed</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260730-migrant-exodus-leaves-south-african-employers-short-handed</link><description>
South Africa is suffering a drop in its workforce, following the departure of thousands of foreign workers in the wake of a wave of xenophobic attacks, anti-migrant protests and intensified immigration enforcement.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/02949208-8b3c-11f1-ad9b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Zimbabweans-leaving-SA-afp-july-2026-000-B9WF6Y3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/02949208-8b3c-11f1-ad9b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Zimbabweans-leaving-SA-afp-july-2026-000-B9WF6Y3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">79de796a-8b31-11f1-be81-9b02f149194f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 08:18:59 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/02949208-8b3c-11f1-ad9b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Zimbabweans-leaving-SA-afp-july-2026-000-B9WF6Y3.jpg">AFP - ZINYANGE AUNTONY</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>EU condemns Iranian 'aggression' against French diplomats</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260729-eu-condemns-iran-aggression-against-french-diplomats</link><description>
The European Union on Tuesday condemned an "aggression" this month by Iranian security services against two French diplomats in Tehran.
